'' Name resolution: references bound to symbols, type references turned into TypeIds,
'' and the parser's deliberately ambiguous call-or-assign node decided.
''
'' The interesting row is 'Add = sum' INSIDE function Add: that is BASIC's result
'' assignment, not an assignment to a variable and not a comparison. The parser cannot
'' know which; the resolver can, because it knows the enclosing procedure.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --resolve tests/symbols/src/resolve.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 unresolved
'' EXPECT-OUT: -> function-result
'' EXPECT-OUT: -> assign
'' EXPECT-OUT: -> call
'' EXPECT-OUT: -> long ptr
'' GOLDEN: expected/resolve.out
